  message: "ADDRESSED ON BRANCH jgstern-agent/fix/sinol (local, not pushed; WI-sinol run 2026-10-01). WI-sinol listed this row as its prerequisite (gating module_exports on is_exported would otherwise drop every CommonJS edge), so the CommonJS half of the JS/TS export scan landed there. Status NOT changed.\n\nWhat the branch does (js_ts.py `_collect_exported_names` -> new `_extract_commonjs_export_names`): top-level assignment statements export a LOCAL binding when the target is `module.exports` (value identifier, or an object literal's shorthand / `key: identifier` / method properties), `exports.k` or `module.exports.k` (value identifier), including chains like express's `exports = module.exports = createApplication`. Bare `exports = f`, `module.exports = require('./x')`, computed `exports[k] = f`, `exports.cfg = { f }` and a guarded (non-top-level) export collect nothing -- each pinned by a test.\n\nShapes from this row's scope list: `module.exports = { f, g }` YES; `module.exports.f = f` YES; `exports.f = f` YES; `module.exports = f` YES; `module.exports = class X {}` NO -- the analyzer emits no symbol for a class expression (filed WI-rabod-rodil-dokok-tagiv-razaz-dilil-salok-havaz); `module.exports = require('./x')` binds no local, nothing to mark.\nResidual export forms (guarded/UMD, Object.assign, Object.defineProperty): WI-kodop-bopup-vutoz-humod-vuzot-zizud-nufut-rikab.\n\nMeasured on sharp (CommonJS): JS functions with is_exported False->True: 29 (lib/is.js 15, lib/libvips.js 12, lib/constructor.js Sharp, test/fixtures getPath), variables 3; 0 True->False. Tests: packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/tests/test_js_ts_export_status.py::TestCommonJsExports."  # c152
